Virtual Experimentation Framework User Manual            {#mainpage}
=============================================

This manual describes how to use the Virtual Experimentation Framework and how to interpret the results obtained from the VEF.
The manual includes:

- \ref user_reference that presents main components of the VEF and discusses how to operate it. User reference describes:
  - \ref sec_expert_mode that provides a complete control over all the knobs in the VEF, and
  - \ref sec_simple_mode that helps to carry out standard tasks with minimal effort, while sticking to pre-defined defaults.   
- \ref guided_tour that gives an step-by-step overview of typical use cases where the VEF is applied.
- \ref examples that summarizes the collection of sample problems bundled with the VEF.

